<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2673"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Zenith<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 24, 2004 - 9:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Api: I was just wondering if you had a documented source somewhere stating that the faucet was NOT on. How do we know he is obviously a fake if we don&#39;t really know whether or not the faucet was on. Looking for solid facts in a sea of opinions. Can you reveal Who says the faucet wasn&#39;t on?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
