<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2835"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 11:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don´t really understand where this number 440 came from except that i read it was from the latest puzzel in the &#34;from BTK&#34; thred, but I found out that there is a polaroid camera named 440 and it was produced from 1971-1976. <BR>Is this the polaroid camera BTK took pictures of his victims with? <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.rwhirled.com/landlist/landdcam-pack.htm" target=_top>http://www.rwhirled.com/landlist/landdcam-pack.htm</a> <BR>&#40;look under series 400&#41; <BR> <BR> Model 440 &#40;&#34;Automatic 440&#34;&#41;:  <BR>Produced: 1971-1976 / Original Retail: $99.95 <BR>Estimated Production: 340,000 - &#40;500,000&#41; <BR>Otherwise similar to Model 340. <BR> <BR> Model 440 &#40;shown with #490 Focused Flash&#41; [JPEG, 31k]  <BR> <BR>skov <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
