<!--Post: 2852--><!--Time: 1104197283-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2852"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lanena<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lanena<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 5:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nugzter:  Yes, the WPD had their own crime scene personel in the 70&#39;s and currently does as well.  However, back then the bodies were typically removed before this individual arrived at the scene.  This is why it is so important to understand the significance of the photos &#40;copies&#41; that were sent to the WPD by BTK.   <BR>To me it seems VERY unlikely that he &#40;BTK&#41; returned to the house to take a picture of Mrs. Wegerle.  THe pictures that were sent to WPD were SEQUENTIAL, meaning that they were taken one after another.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2852-->
<!--Post: 2859--><!--Time: 1104203465-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2859"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 7:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Glad, You and I have the same feeling about BTK and Zodiac being the same old killer. He just changed his way of collecting slaves, like he said he would.Zodiac wasn&#39;t front page news after a while here.I believe he moved around from state to state back in the 70s,we didn&#39;t hear from Z for a few years until just after the Otero&#39;s were killed then on Jan 29th 74 a letter was sent again. He &#40;BTK&#41; likes the number 3,did you know the number 3 was on a sign at the murder site on Lake Herman Rd. coincidence ? maybe.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2859-->
<!--Post: 2862--><!--Time: 1104206577-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2862"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 8:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->LANENA wrote:  &#34;To me it seems VERY unlikely that he &#40;BTK&#41; returned to the house to take a picture of Mrs. Wegerle. THe pictures that were sent to WPD were SEQUENTIAL, meaning that they were taken one after another.&#34; <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t understand. The fact that BLT may have come back to take a final photo doesn&#39;t mess up the fact that the photos he sent in were also SEQUENTIAL. Think about it. That final photo may indeed have been the last in BLTs&#39; SEQUENCE of pictures.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
