<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3328"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->C<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 7:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Regarding the &#34;440&#34; code, using simple substitution as follows. <BR> <BR>C = &#39;t&#39;, V = &#39;o&#39;, N = &#39;b&#39;, T = &#39;k&#39;, A = &#39;d&#39;, H = &#39;i&#39;, W = &#39;_&#39; <BR>D = &#39;m&#39;, E = &#39;a&#39;, F = &#39;s&#39;, R = &#39;l&#39;, L = &#39;o&#39;, B = &#39;d&#39;, S = &#39;_&#39; <BR>K = &#39;_&#39;, O = &#39;_&#39;, I = &#39;s&#39;, X = &#39;_&#39;, Y = &#39;_&#39;, M = &#39;n&#39;, Q = &#39;y&#39; <BR>P = &#39;_&#39;, Z = &#39;_&#39; <BR> <BR>Turns the code of: <BR> <BR>CVNCTAHAWYDAEAFNRLLBQDHIIHLM24BTS9NK24VPOIXYFWDMLZ PCCLZFVYHAKMSTP <BR> <BR>in to: <BR> <BR>tobtkdid__mdadsbloodymission24dk_9b_24o__s__s_mno_ _tto_so_id_n_k_ <BR> <BR>or  <BR> <BR>to btk did ??m dads bloody mission 24 dk? 9 b? 24 o??s??s?mno? ?tto?so?id?n?k? <BR> <BR>I&#39;d hammer on the rest of it but I smell a hoax. Of course I could be way off in the weeds... <BR> <BR>- C<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3328-->
<!--Post: 3335--><!--Time: 1104812158-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3335"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 8:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In posts by &#34;-&#34; in the &#34;From BTK thread&#34; I see the #s at the begining of the code in the first one &amp; broken up but still present in the third post by &#34;-&#34;, contain the &#34;offender #&#34; of the man currently in prison, in Oregon for a simular murder of a family of 4 that occured right after the Otero murder. <BR> <BR>Wichita Police investigated the murders in Oregon committed by Colin Hockings, a man who also fit the discription of a man seen leaving the Otero Home after the murders. <BR> <BR>Police concluded that there was no link between the two multiple murders. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>Colin Hockings Prison # 3544533 <BR> <BR>The #s at the begining &#40;-the letters&#41; from: Messages from BTK thread here: 54434353  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/264/129.html?1104640989" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/264/129.ht ml?1104640989</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
