<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3780"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 08, 2005 - 3:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->All these interesting posts from people who claim to know the identity of BTK &#40;i.e. Tony, Tim, Trent C. &amp; Luis Cypher etc...&#41; are very interesting. However, anyone that has read case history, profiles etc. could could embelish the known facts and even make them believeable. <BR> <BR>My point is this. The person&#40;s&#41; posting these messages want us to believe them. Don&#39;t you? You&#39;re not just posting here because you have nothing better to do, or are you? The problem is nobody believes you. Should they? You can say you don&#39;t care... I believe different. <BR> <BR>I challenge you to prove you have intamate knowledge of BTK. Tell us something that we don&#39;t already know and couldn&#39;t be made up. I mean c&#39;mon, you get off thinking of all the cyber slueths rushing to research obituaries when you posted that BTK offed his mother. You and I both know that&#39;s going no where. Even if he did, her death was obviously not considered a homicide. I could give several suggestions but just use your imagination, you&#39;re good at that right? <BR> <BR>I know you will not give up your identity &#40;or BTKs for that matter&#41; but let&#39;s stop screwing around with stuff that I could post myself. Or, do you actually know anything more than others that have followed the story. <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
